# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, and checked out as LF
# everywhere including Windows.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf enabled rewrites every
# file to CRLF on checkout. Nothing breaks, but every commit prints a warning
# and any tool that compares bytes rather than lines sees a difference that is
# not there. Declaring it once removes the question from the project.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that are bytes, not text: never touched, never diffed as lines.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated: keep it out of diffs and reviews, it is not read by people.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
